nt to mention that back in march we  got our first reports from ming chu quo  that the iphone 13 lineup would be  getting bigger batteries by using a new  space-saving design for some of the  internal parts and back in june we got  another report that mentioned the exact  battery sizes of the iphone 13 lineup  with a pro max model going from 38.76  milliamp hours to a massive 43.52  the 13 and 13 pro going from 2815 to  3095 and the mini going from 2227  to 24.06 so the biggest difference is  going to be seen on the iphone 13 pro  max model going further the a15 bionic  chip is expected to improve efficiency  in battery life on top of that extra  battery size improvement so i think the  iphone 13 lineup is gonna kill it in  terms of battery life now one of the  biggest problems we currently have with  the iphone 12 lineup especially the  iphone 12 pro max is overheating while  out in the sun playing games or just  wirelessly charging and because of this  overheating issue the graphics  performance of the a14 chip in the  iphone 12 is much lower than on the ipad  air 4 which uses the same exact a14 chip  this basically means that apple is being  forced to slow down the gpu cores on the  a14 to keep it from overheating which it  already is which means that the a15 chip  will likely also get thermally throttled  even if it's supposed to be more  powerful and efficient but thankfully  there are reports that apple is working  on a new vapor chamber cooling system  for the iphone but it's not clear if  it's going to be ready for this year's  iphones but i honestly think that apple  has no choice but to add this feature  this year because of the huge  overheating problems on the iphone 12 so  let's hope for that and interestingly  apple has reportedly ordered a hundred  million a15 chips for the iphone 13  lineup which is incredible showing that  apple themselves are expecting to sell  massive amounts of iphone 13 models now  i know you're gonna say that the a14  chip is already powerful enough and  there's really no point to making it  more powerful with the a15 chip but what  most people don't realize is that the  camera greatly depends on the chip's  performance and it's the very reason why  the iphone 12 pro's cameras work so  incredibly well and with that i want to  finally get into the one new feature  that is going to revolutionize the  entire industry and be the most  important factor for upgrading to the  iphone 13 pro three weeks ago i made a  video talking about why lidar is apple's  master plan for the iphone 13 pro and in  that video i mentioned leaks about apple  getting a 2nd gen lidar scanner for the  new iphone which was also visible on the  leaked dummy units of the iphone 13 pro  models which showed a much larger  lighter scanner on the camera bump but  the point of the video was that apple is  finally adding portrait video mode with  background blur based on a leak from max  weinbach earlier this year and this  feature is gonna work in real time just  like apple's new facetime blur feature  works but on the iphone 13 it's also  gonna allow you to disable the blur or  adjust the strength in post after you  film it which has never been seen before  and i even showed you guys the brand new  apple patents that describe how apple  will be compressing the 3d depth map  data using a new hardware chip to allow  this to work and with that said just a  couple of days ago mark german actually  confirmed my prediction by saying that  the iphone 13 pro models will be getting  this new portrait mode video feature  alongside a new prores format for video  recording and this feature should also  be coming to the selfie camera because  there are rumors that the smaller notch  is going to be due to a new 2nd gen  facetime sensor array which also uses  lidar technology now i personally  believe that this feature will  revolutionize the smartphone industry  just like the original portrait mode for  photos did way back in the day and 